# NO-TRACKING environment for the bashy victoria-logs verified build.
# Shell-sourceable; shipped as a release asset so a launcher applies exactly
# what this build was gated against. Every knob is documented in
# builds/victoria-logs/README.md with its upstream source at the pinned tag.
#
# Usage: set -a; . bashy-build/no-tracking.env; set +a
#
# victoria-logs has NO update checker and NO usage reporting, and it reads
# flags rather than the environment (upstream only consults $VAR for a flag
# when -envflag.enable is passed, which bashy never passes). The no-tracking
# surface is therefore a FLAG policy the launcher must honour:
#
# MUST pass:
#   -httpListenAddr=127.0.0.1:<port>   upstream default is :9428 — EVERY interface
#   -storageDataPath=<data dir>        keep state inside the service's own dir
#
# MUST NOT pass:
#   -pushmetrics.url=<url>             remote write of /metrics to a third party
#                                      (lib/pushmetrics, upstream default: empty)
#
# files/no-egress-test.sh is what proves the policy held for THIS build.
#
# Go's net/http honours the proxy environment, so an operator shell that
# exports a proxy would hand the service an egress path it never asked for.
# Clearing all three and allowing only loopback in NO_PROXY closes that door.
HTTP_PROXY=
HTTPS_PROXY=
http_proxy=
https_proxy=
ALL_PROXY=
all_proxy=
NO_PROXY=127.0.0.1,::1,localhost
no_proxy=127.0.0.1,::1,localhost
